    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0282" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.60d Finnish Vessels/153</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Finnish Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Järnefelt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-04">March 4, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In your note of February 1, 1935, you
                    communicated to me the information that a complete record regarding the claims
                    for the detention of thirteen Finnish sailing vessels was handed to the Legal
                    Adviser of the Department on January 30, 1935.</p>
                <p>I now inform you that the answer of the United States to the claim growing out of
                    the alleged detention by the United States of thirteen Finnish sailing vessels
                    was today handed in triplicate to Doctor Sigurd von Numers, Secretary of your
                        Legation.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d160-f1"/></p>
                <p>In view of the answer handed to Doctor von Numers, it is not deemed necessary
                    specifically to answer your predecessor’s note of December 20, 1934,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d160-f2"/> relating to the claim. The answer handed to <pb
                        facs="0283" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/> Doctor von Numers may be regarded as an
                    answer to any question raised in the note of December 20, 1934, as well as to
                    other questions dealt with in the answer of the United States.</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walton Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
